% Test cases for the canes and crutches policy (canes_crutches.le):
% synthetic claims, one per criterion of LCD L33733 and per code the LCD
% leaves without coverage. Findings are recorded as the treating
% practitioner's, a medical reviewer's or the Council's; a finding nobody
% made leaves the answer conditional. A cane or crutch is a purchase: no
% rental month.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base canes_crutches cases includes these resources:
    canes_crutches.

the knowledge base canes_crutches cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete claim for a quad cane (E0105): the three findings, the standard
% written order communicated before the date of service, the delivery and
% its proof.
scenario quad_cane_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the quad cane.
    the HCPCS code of the quad cane is "E0105".
    the quad cane is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "right hemiparesis after a stroke prevents walking to the bathroom without support".
    the finding walking aid can be safely used about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aid sufficiently resolves mobility deficit about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the quad cane is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the quad cane is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the quad cane includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the quad cane includes order date.
    the order for the quad cane includes description of the item.
    the order for the quad cane includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the quad cane includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the quad cane was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the quad cane was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the quad cane.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% Criterion 1 fails: the medical reviewer finds no significant mobility
% limitation in the record.
scenario no_mobility_limitation is:
    claim 1 is for the crutches.
    the HCPCS code of the crutches is "E0114".
    the crutches is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Ben is unsupported, according to the medical reviewer, because "the record documents independent ambulation in the home without assistance".
    the finding walking aid can be safely used about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aid sufficiently resolves mobility deficit about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% Criterion 2 fails: the beneficiary cannot use a crutch safely.
scenario cannot_use_safely is:
    claim 1 is for the forearm crutch.
    the HCPCS code of the forearm crutch is "E0111".
    the forearm crutch is furnished to Cy.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aid can be safely used about Cy is unsupported, according to the medical reviewer, because "the record documents severe bilateral hand weakness and two falls while using a crutch".
    the finding walking aid sufficiently resolves mobility deficit about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].

% Criterion 3 not decided: nothing in the record says whether a cane would
% resolve the deficit, so the answer is conditional on that finding.
scenario resolution_not_decided is:
    claim 1 is for the cane.
    the HCPCS code of the cane is "E0100".
    the cane is furnished to Dee.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aid can be safely used about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding walking aid sufficiently resolves mobility deficit about Dee is established"].

% The Council finds a cane would not resolve the deficit: the record shows
% the beneficiary needs a walker, so criterion 3 is unsupported.
scenario cane_insufficient_council is:
    claim 1 is for the cane.
    the HCPCS code of the cane is "E0100".
    the cane is furnished to Eve.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aid can be safely used about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aid sufficiently resolves mobility deficit about Eve is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the treating practitioner's own note states that the beneficiary requires bilateral support and cannot ambulate in the home with a single cane".
    rn expects answers [].

% An articulating spring assisted crutch (E0117) and a crutch substitute
% (E0118): in scope, never reasonable and necessary.
scenario articulating_crutch_and_substitute is:
    claim 1 is for the articulating crutch.
    the HCPCS code of the articulating crutch is "E0117".
    the articulating crutch is furnished to Fay.
    the residence of Fay is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 2 is for the crutch substitute.
    the HCPCS code of the crutch substitute is "E0118".
    the crutch substitute is furnished to Fay.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aid can be safely used about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aid sufficiently resolves mobility deficit about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% Reasonable and necessary, but no proof of delivery: payable fails at the
% remedy.
scenario no_proof_of_delivery is:
    claim 1 is for the crutches.
    the HCPCS code of the crutches is "E0114".
    the crutches is furnished to Gus.
    the residence of Gus is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the finding significant mobility limitation about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "a fractured ankle in a cast".
    the finding walking aid can be safely used about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding walking aid sufficiently resolves mobility deficit about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the crutches is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the crutches is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the crutches includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the crutches includes order date.
    the order for the crutches includes description of the item.
    the order for the crutches includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the crutches includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the crutches was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the crutches was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the supplier holds proof of delivery for the crutches"]].
